    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "This expression is obtained by noting that $W(z)$ is a weighting factor for phenotype $z$. The denominator is the mean individual fitness, $\\overline{W}$. Letting the relative fitness of phenotype $z$ be $w(z) = W(z)/\\overline{W}$, Equation 3.19 simplifies to $p_{s}(z) = w(z)p(z)$. It follows that the mean phenotype after selection is",
