      "content_sha256": "5f76542d2481cbaa5f43d4b6f5d026b3c7ff229db22c2d14efb0d0b7f20240cd"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "where $ \\mu_{o} $ is the mean phenotype of the offspring of the selected parents. This fundamental relationship, known as the breeders' equation, combines information on the forces of selection (S) with that on inheritance ( $ \\beta $) to yield a predictive equation for evolutionary change across generations. A genetic interpretation of the regression coefficient $ \\beta $ will be provided in the final example of this chapter.",
